Intercom reliability and lifecycle qualification

Workstream ID: ic-07
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/6
Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: Recoverable background jobs and safe desktop/audio lifecycle
Dependencies: ic-06

Purpose:
  Qualify failure and lifecycle behavior after the first slice, without treating
  a successful demo as a production-ready or publishable assistant.

Tasks:
  [ ] Test restart/reconnect, lost acknowledgment and duplicate/out-of-order events.
  [ ] Verify per-session serialization and shared-workspace conflict handling.
  [ ] Qualify audio/device/provider failures and resource use with the live graph.
  [ ] Compare priority profiles under load and verify saved/default settings.
  [ ] Define tray close, explicit exit, sleep/resume and task ownership behavior.
  [ ] Verify retention/deletion, credential boundaries and notification recovery.
  [ ] Document supported limits, recovery instructions and separate release gates.

Acceptance criteria:
  Uncertain dispatch is never blindly retried and no false done is spoken.
  Recovery preserves receipts without claiming exactly-once audible delivery.
  User-owned sessions/processes and unsaved work remain protected.
  Only identified Intercom-owned processes can be stopped by cleanup.
  Privacy/resource targets are measured on the selected configuration.
  Speed-first behavior remains correct under load; quality/accuracy trade-offs
  and profile-switch boundaries are measured rather than assumed.
  No autostart, service activation, commit, release or deployment is implied.

Completion evidence:
  None. Qualification depends on a separately authorized implemented ic-06.

Completion log:
  2026-11-10 - Added future qualification scope under architecture-only authority.
